<title>UK: Deutsche sets warrants on seven German stocks.</title>
<headline>Deutsche sets warrants on seven German stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>DB Capital Markets has issued American-style call and put warrants in marks, of 500,000 per tranche on shares of seven blue chip German stocks, lead manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell said.</p>
<p>There are warrants on shares of Allianz AG Holding, Continental AG, Daimler-Benz AG, Merck KGaA, Muenchener Rueckversicherungs-Gesellschaft, PREUSSAG AG and Schering AG.</p>
<p>The warrants all mature on June 18, 1998 and the payment date is February 27, 1997. They are listed on the Frankfurt and Deusseldorf exchanges and available in minimum lots of 100.</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
